Offer window sources to every monitor screencast request.

Some apps call SelectSources with types=MONITOR only; Steam Remote
Play's PipeWire capture (steam -pipewire) does, so its picker shows
only monitors. On niri, the switchable "niri Dynamic Cast Target" is
exposed as a window, so such apps could never select it. Whenever
monitors are requested, also allow windows. The widened types are
stored on the session, so restoring a saved window selection passes
validation too.

--- a/src/screencast.c
+++ b/src/screencast.c
@@ -732,6 +732,11 @@
   if (!g_variant_lookup (arg_options, "types", "u", &types))
     types = SCREEN_CAST_SOURCE_TYPE_MONITOR;
 
+  /* Offer windows to every monitor request, so the picker always lists
+   * niri's "Dynamic Cast Target" pseudo-window. */
+  if (types & SCREEN_CAST_SOURCE_TYPE_MONITOR)
+    types |= SCREEN_CAST_SOURCE_TYPE_WINDOW;
+
   if (!(types & (SCREEN_CAST_SOURCE_TYPE_MONITOR |
                  SCREEN_CAST_SOURCE_TYPE_WINDOW |
                  SCREEN_CAST_SOURCE_TYPE_VIRTUAL)))
